    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12-a2-a2">

                <pb facs="0111" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg21"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">official dispatch.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santa Rosa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 8<hi
                                rendition="#italic">th</hi>, 1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that last night at 12 o’clock I advanced on the enemy’s flank with
                    artillery and reached his rear guard. At dawn I was ready, in spite of the
                    darkness, the difficulty of the operation, and the uneven character of the
                    ground. Arredondo had to leave his intrenchments and face me.</p>
                <p>At 6 o’clock in the morning I attacked him. At half-past 8 o’clock he was routed,
                    and he and all his officers and infantry prisoners, as also part of his cavalry,
                    the rest escaping, having good horses.</p>
                <p>The battle lasted two hours. It was bloody, and we have to deplore heavy losses,
                    among them Col. Carlos Paz, who fell in front of the Third of the line, pierced
                    by twelve bullets. Commander Timote fell in the thick of the enemy’s ranks, and
                    many other officers, whose names I will forward to your excellency.</p>
                <p>I beg to recommend to the government all the chiefs, officers, and men of this
                    army, especially Lieut. Col. Edward Racedo and Colonel Nelson.</p>
                <p>I will send on details, and meanwhile congratulate your excellency on the
                    pacification of the republic.</p>
                <closer><signed>JULIO A. ROCA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
